        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26078826?u=9388a2c2a0f1ca2799a4fd23f3e060c353d6ac37&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarify behavior when passing an invalid or revoked object URL.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently this info is not specified, and one might expect the method to throw in such cases. It turns out it's quite useful that it <em>doesn't</em> throw, as it allows common patterns such as revoking any extant object URL before creating a new one:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"let currentObjectUrl = ''\n\nfunction doSomething(blob) {\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(currentObjectUrl)\n    currentObjectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n    // use currentObjectUrl for something\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">currentObjectUrl</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">''</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">doSomething</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">blob</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">URL</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">revokeObjectURL</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">currentObjectUrl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-s1\">currentObjectUrl</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">URL</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">createObjectURL</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">blob</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\">// use currentObjectUrl for something</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/FileAPI/#dfn-revokeObjectURL\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/FileAPI/#dfn-revokeObjectURL</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note: This means that rather than throwing some kind of error, attempting to revoke a URL that isn’t registered or that was registered from an environment in a different storage partition will silently fail. User agents might display a message on the error console if this happens.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In practice, no browser/environment I checked actually does print a console message on failure.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42867",
            "title": "Add note on revoking invalid object URLs",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-22T13:12:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-22T13:10:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "lionel-rowe",
                "url": "https://github.com/lionel-rowe"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178316747?u=6b1468b0b83d96ee9bff1af215f7494c4165ca55&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">###Description</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR corrects the “Allowable properties” section for the ::highlight pseudo-element.<br>\nIt removes vendor-prefixed properties and updates the list to use the standard stroke-color, fill-color, and stroke-width properties.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">###Motivation</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The MDN page currently lists -webkit-text-* properties as allowable, which does not match the CSS specification.<br>\nThis change aligns the documentation with the spec and prevents developers from relying on unsupported properties.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">###Related issues and pull requests</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42863.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3841973692\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42863\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42863/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42863\">#42863</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42866",
            "title": "Fix allowable properties for ::highlight pseudo-element",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-24T22:00:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-22T12:11:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "SURYAS1306",
                "url": "https://github.com/SURYAS1306"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178316747?u=6b1468b0b83d96ee9bff1af215f7494c4165ca55&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">###Description</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change clarifies the blur event documentation to note that browser behavior differs when a focused element is removed from the document.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, Chromium-based browsers fire a blur event in this case, while Firefox does not.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">###Motivation</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page previously stated that blur is not fired when a focused element is removed from the document, which is only true for Firefox.<br>\nThis update prevents confusion by documenting the cross-browser difference reported in issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3823377990\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42801/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801\">#42801</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">###Related issues and pull requests</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42801.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3823377990\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42801/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801\">#42801</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42864",
            "title": "Clarify blur event behavior when focused element is removed",
